- Venlo - 40 uur - € 18,70 per uur 
Are you looking for a challenging position as a Reachstacker Driver in Venlo? Do you enjoy working with heavy equipment and keeping a cool head in a dynamic terminal environment? At the terminal in Greenport Venlo, containers from sea, road, and rail come together. You ensure that everything is handled safely, efficiently, and on time. No container is too heavy, and no schedule is too tight. Thanks to your experience and expertise, the terminal keeps moving day and night 
What do we offer? 
• An hourly wage of €17,47, including shift allowances; 
• Working in a 2-shift system between 06:00 and 00:00; 
• Working one Saturday every four weeks, compensated as time off in lieu; 
• A solid pension scheme; 
• Full travel allowance of €0.23 per kilometre; 
• The opportunity to work with modern and well-maintained equipment; 
• Career development opportunities within a growing family-owned company; 
• A varied position in a professional terminal environment. 
What will you do? - Load and unload containers from trucks and rail wagons; - Move and correctly position containers in the stack using the reachstacker; - Occasionally operate the terminal tractor to move trailers; - Coordinate with planning, gate operations, and colleagues on the terminal; - Monitor safety, quality, and efficiency at all times; - Respond quickly to changes in the planning; - Work in a 2-shift schedule. 
What do you bring? - Experience as a Reachstacker Driver is a strong advantage; - No reachstacker experience yet, but affinity with logistics and experience operating a forklift or reach truck? We also encourage you to apply; - You take responsibility for your work and your machine; - You remain calm and flexible when situations change; - You have a good command of Dutch or, at the very least, good English communication skills; - You are willing to work in shifts; - Safety is always your top priority. 
Interested in applying? Please ...

Do you already have some experience in purchasing, supply chain, or logistics and are you ready for the next step in your career? Would you like to work in a unique technical environment? Then this position as an Aviation Procurement Coordinator could be the perfect opportunity for you.

As an Aviation Procurement Coordinator, you ensure that the right parts are available at the right time for aircraft maintenance. You will be responsible for placing and following up on purchase orders, monitoring delivery schedules, and ensuring that all administrative processes are handled accurately. Thanks to your efforts, maintenance activities can be carried out according to plan.

You will work closely with buyers, suppliers, and technical colleagues on a daily basis. This will not only give you valuable insight into purchasing processes but also allow you to develop knowledge of aircraft maintenance and the international aviation industry. This role is ideal for someone with a solid foundation in purchasing who wants to further develop into a specialized procurement professional.

You will work closely with experienced Buyers, Senior Buyers, and maintenance technicians on a daily basis, giving you the opportunity to gain a broad understanding of both the organization and the industry.

We are looking for someone who is eager to learn, takes responsibility, and works with great attention to detail.

In addition, you have:

- MBO+ or Bachelor's level working and thinking ability;
- Proven experience in purchasing activities, such as placing orders, communicating with suppliers, and monitoring delivery schedules;
- Good command of the English language, both spoken and written;
- Experience with administrative processes and digital systems (experience with ERP systems is an advantage);
- A structured and detail-oriented way of working;
- A proactive mindset and the perseverance to find solutions when challenges arise;
